"""English source copy: explain decisions and interactions, not field lists."""
SIMULATION = "Defaults for every simulation. They take effect the next time you press Start and apply to all bodies that do not use their own simulation settings."
SHOW_COLLIDERS = "Collision shapes are the simplified geometry Newton uses for contact: a box, a sphere or a convex hull around each body. They appear as coloured outlines over the model and reveal where contact geometry differs from what you see. This option decides whether the display is on when a window opens; the menu command “Show collision shapes” switches it in the current window. The display never changes how bodies collide."
COLLIDER_SHORTCUT = "Opens IngeTrazo's shortcut settings at the command that switches the collision display. No shortcut is assigned by default."
KEY_SLOTS = "Key slots are commands that bindings in the control panel can use to move actuators and virtual controls with the keyboard. A label (for example \"Gripper\") is shown with the slot in IngeTrazo's shortcut settings and in the bindings. Assign… opens IngeTrazo's shortcut settings at the slot; no key is assigned by default. A slot only reacts while a simulation runs, so its key stays free for modelling."
KEY_BINDINGS_AXIS = "A key slot can move this axis while a simulation runs. An axis has at most one binding; one slot may serve several. Bindings are saved with the model and can be changed only while no simulation runs. Virtual controls are bound on their cards in the control panel."
KEY_BINDING_SLOT = "The key slot that operates this control. Its key is assigned in the preferences under Key slots."
KEY_BINDING_MODE = "Toggle: a press switches between two values. Step: each press adds the step; a second slot can subtract it."
KEY_BINDING_VALUE = "The value a press sets."
KEY_BINDING_REST = "The value a press returns to when the control is at the value above."
KEY_BINDING_STEP = "The amount each press adds, limited to the range the control panel offers."
KEY_BINDING_DOWN = "An optional second slot that subtracts the step."
KEY_SLOT_LABEL = "A name for what this slot operates, for example \"Gripper\". It is saved in the settings for every model and shown next to the slot number."
KEY_SLOT_COUNT ="Adds a slot after the last one or removes the last one, at once. Removing a slot also clears its key and label. Bindings that refer to a slot that no longer exists are skipped at Start, not deleted."
GRAVITY = "Acceleration along the model's Z axis in m/s². −9.81 is Earth's gravity, 0 makes all bodies weightless and positive values pull upwards. Stronger gravity means more load for actuators."
GROUND = "Adds an invisible, infinite floor at height Z = 0 for bodies to land on. Switch it off when parts should move below Z = 0 or when the model has its own base."
WARN_GROUND = "At Start, the control panel lists movable bodies that reach below Z = 0 while ground contact is on: they scrape along the ground and distort the result. Bodies that only rest on Z = 0, fixed bodies and bodies without ground contact are not listed. The warning never prevents the start."
VIRTUAL_CONTROLS = "A virtual control moves several axes with one switch or slider, for example \"Flap: closed / open\". Each state sets a target for every axis in the control; a slider moves smoothly from state to state. Axes in a virtual control have no control of their own in the control panel. Virtual controls are saved with the model and can be changed only while no simulation runs."
MANAGED_BY_VIRTUAL_CONTROL = "Opens the virtual control editor on the control that moves this axis. Available only while no simulation runs."
KEEP_POSE = "Reset writes the simulated position and rotation of the bodies into the model instead of restoring the original pose, as one undo step; their axes and attachments move along. Joint start angles are not changed. If a body cannot simply be moved (flexible, locked or containing groups) or the geometry changed, nothing is kept and the original model is restored. Resetting after an error never keeps the pose."
KEEP_WARNINGS = "Reset keeps the last warning or error in the control panel, with its list of bodies, instead of replacing it with the reset notice. The bodies in the list can then be selected in the model. Start always clears every message and checks again."
LINEAR_DAMPING = "Slows down moving bodies, similar to air resistance. At 1 /s a free body loses about two thirds of its speed per second; 0 switches damping off. More damping calms oscillations but also resists intended motion, so actuators need more force."
ANGULAR_DAMPING = "Like linear damping, but for rotation: slows down spinning and wobbling bodies. 0 switches it off."
QUALITY = "How exactly joints and contacts are solved. Quick suits setting up large mechanisms, Balanced everyday work, and Precise checking demanding contacts. Geometry and cable resolution stay the same, but motion can differ slightly between the levels."
HIDDEN_GEOMETRY = "Hidden groups and groups on hidden layers. When needed simulates a hidden body only if a visible body depends on it, for example as its reference body, attachment, connection or coupling, and keeps hidden static bodies as surroundings. All other hidden bodies are left out, so large models start faster. Always simulates every hidden body; Never leaves all of them out."
RUNTIME_SETUP = "Creates the runtime in your IngeTrazo data folder: a private Python 3.12 and MuJoCo 3.3.7. It starts only when you confirm. Remove runtime is offered only for a runtime created this way and deletes only that folder."
RUNTIME_MANUAL = "Use this when the automatic setup is not available or you want to keep your own Python environment. The guide covers Linux, Windows and Flatpak. Afterwards enter the interpreter under Python with MuJoCo above."
RUNTIME = "The Python interpreter of the environment that contains MuJoCo 3.3.7. Newton runs the simulation and the collision display in it as a separate process. Change this only when that environment has been moved or replaced; editing the model never requires it. Check runtime tests the interpreter entered here."
PROFILES = "A profile is a saved set of body and axis values. Applying it copies the values onto a body; the body keeps them until you sync it again."
BODY = "Mass, friction and bounce decide how this body reacts to forces and contacts. Heavier bodies need more actuator force."
COLLISION_SHAPE = "Newton uses a simple shape for contacts, not your exact model. Pick the shape that fits the body best."
MOTION = "A servo holds a position, a motor holds a speed. Max. force, load and contacts decide what the body actually reaches."
LIMIT_HARDNESS = "How hard the stops are. 100 % is a solid stop; lower values give way under load like a rubber buffer."
CONNECTION = "Joins this body to another at a point, for example a connecting rod to a slider. The joint must not block the motion of your axes."
FLEXIBLE = "Turns one open line into a rope or cable that bends and swings. Select a group that holds just that line."
COLLISIONS = "Lets this body pass through the bodies you pick, for example a pin inside its bearing that would otherwise jam. Their joint must then guide them; other contacts stay."
OVERRIDES = "Grey values are inherited from the global settings. Change a value to use it for this body only; the button next to it resets it."
FIELDS = "Attraction pulls other bodies towards this one. With a sideways start velocity it makes an orbit."
COUPLING_FREE = "Makes this axis follow another one, for example two gripper jaws moved by one control. The limits of both axes apply."
COUPLING_FOLLOWER = "This axis follows another axis. Direction and ratio set how it moves with it; the followed axis's actuator drives both."
COUPLING_LEADER = "{bodies} follow this control. Their additional load and limits also affect the leading axis; select a follower to change how far or in which direction it moves."
PROFILE_OVERRIDES = "Values set here are copied to a body when you apply this profile. Grey values stay at the global default; change a value to store it, the button next to it resets it."
TIP_PROFILE_APPLY = "Copies a saved set of body and axis values onto this body."
TIP_PROFILE_STATUS = "In sync: same as the profile. Local changes: this body differs from it. Profile changed: the profile was edited since."
TIP_PROFILE_SYNC = "Copy the profile's values onto this body again. Placement and reference body stay."
TIP_PROFILE_UNLINK = "Keeps the values but stops tracking the profile."
TIP_BEHAVIOUR = "Movable bodies move under gravity and forces. Fixed bodies stay put but others can touch them. Excluded bodies are left out completely."
TIP_REFERENCE = "The body this one hangs on. With an axis it moves relative to that body; without one it stays rigidly attached."
TIP_CONTROL_NAME = "The name of this axis in the control panel."
TIP_ACTUATOR = "Free: nothing drives the axis. Servo: moves to a target position. Motor: runs at a target speed."
TIP_LIMITS = "How far the axis may move either way from where you placed it. Zero is the placed position."
TIP_TARGET = "Where the servo aims, or how fast the motor runs, when the simulation starts. The control panel changes it afterwards."
TIP_SPEED = "Top speed of the axis. A servo never travels faster to its target."
TIP_ACCELERATION = "How quickly the axis gets up to speed."
TIP_DECELERATION = "How quickly the axis slows down."
TIP_FORCE = "The most force the actuator may use (turning force on a rotation axis). If it is too low, the axis lags behind its target under load."
TIP_COUPLING_AXIS = "Only servo axes of the same kind (rotation or linear) can be followed."
TIP_COUPLING_DIRECTION = "Opposite makes this axis move the other way, as with two gripper jaws."
TIP_COUPLING_RATIO = "How far this axis moves when the followed axis moves 1. 2 means twice as far."
TIP_CONNECTION_TYPE = "Ball joint turns freely in every direction. Pin joint turns around one axis. Fixed connection allows no movement."
TIP_CONNECTION_POINT = "Where the joint sits in the model."
TIP_CONNECTION_AXIS = "The direction the pin points along; the bodies turn around it."
TIP_FLEX_MATERIAL = "Rope bends easily, Cable is stiffer. Rigid switches the strand off."
TIP_FLEX_RADIUS = "Thickness of the strand. Thicker means stiffer."
TIP_FLEX_BEND = "How strongly the strand resists bending. Rope and Cable set typical values."
TIP_FLEX_TWIST = "How strongly the strand resists twisting."
TIP_FLEX_DAMPING = "How quickly swinging dies down."
TIP_FLEX_START = "Clamped holds the start end fixed. Pinned holds it in place but lets it swing. Free does not hold it."
TIP_FLEX_END = "Optionally attaches the other end to a body."
TIP_SHAPE = "Box and Sphere are simple shapes. Convex hull wraps the body like cling film and fills dents and holes. Child components use each part on its own, so openings stay open."
TIP_MASS = "How heavy the body is. Heavier parts need stronger actuators."
TIP_FRICTION = "How well surfaces grip. 0 is like ice."
TIP_BOUNCE = "How much the body springs back after a hit. 0 means none; the result is approximate."
TIP_GRAVITY = "Fall acceleration for this body. Z = −9.81 is Earth; all three at 0 make it weightless. It still pulls on connected bodies."
TIP_LINEAR_DAMPING = "Slows the body like air resistance. 0 means no slowing."
TIP_ANGULAR_DAMPING = "The same for spinning."
TIP_GROUND = "Adds an invisible floor at Z = 0 for this body."
TIP_ATTRACTION = "How strongly this body pulls other bodies towards it. 0 means no pull."
TIP_SOFTENING = "Stops the pull from becoming huge at very small distances."
TIP_VELOCITY = "Speed at the start. Only used for movable bodies without an axis or reference body."
